  "body": "Found while the v0.24.0 cut gate was red (run 44362577581). Three `#[ignore]`d tests pinned to #1950 failed the release tier.\n\nWhat happens:\n- A test that is red on purpose looks the same as a broken test. The release tier runs each `--ignored` test, and `xtask` cannot skip a known failure.\n- PR #2035 and PR #2485 added tests that were red from the start. They used a plain `#[ignore]`.\n- The cut needed a one-off skip list in `xtask` to pass.\n\nExpected:\n- `xtask` has one known-fail marker. It names the blocked issue.\n- The gate prints `SKIPPED (known fail, #N): <test>`.\n- The gate fails when a marked test passes, when its issue closes, or when the test fails for a different reason (a crash, another assert).\n- A test that is born red does not land as a plain `#[ignore]`. The review rules say so.\n- `cargo xtask release` runs the same issue check as `cut.yml` (`release.rs:186-194` does not run it now).\n\nMaintainer, 2026-11-18: \"yes file all 3 changes and move them to P4\".\n\nDone means: the one-off skip list of the v0.24.0 cut is replaced by this marker, and a test pins each rule above.\n\nProcess change: yes.\n",
